			"Message": "fix(Output): Strip backtick quoting from JSDoc to fix esbuild parse error\n\nesbuild's JSDoc parser does not accept backtick-delimited inline code in `/** */` comments — encountering e.g. \\`vscode-file://\\` triggers `Expected \";\" but found \"word\"`. Strip all escaped backtick quoting (`\\`word\\`` → `word`) and replace bare backticks with single quotes across the InjectWebviewBlobUrlRewrite JSDoc block.\n\nThis is the scripted fix applied via `fix_backticks.py`, which is committed alongside for reproducibility.\n\nAlso expose `ITestService` in ExposeAccessor (aligned with the existing Debug/CustomEditor pattern), enabling the Celestia test runner to resolve via WorkspaceAccessor. Fix a comment apostrophe style for consistency.",
			"SHA": "8280a620d30bd9be2d9880a505bd17e100141852"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T23:17:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				360,
				17
			],
			"Message": "style(Output): Normalize whitespace and fix trailing blank lines across shim runtime\n\nStandardize code style across the low-level intercept layer and diagnostics pipeline by adding consistent blank lines after declarations, removing stray blank lines before closing brackets, and reflowing long conditionals that exceeded the 80-column guide.\n\nKey changes:\n- Add missing blank lines after `let`/`const` declarations in all seven LandDiagnostics record functions, flushAll(), forceFlush(), and across all six Intercept proxies (ErrorHandler, EmitterFire, Cancellation, Disposable, Async, Timing)\n- Fix trailing blank lines in parenthesized conditions throughout Hook.ts and the Webview Blob URL Rewrite\n- Collapse the `InjectShimHook` import to the correct alphabetical position in Plugin/Index.ts (moved down one line after ExposeWorkbenchAccessor group)\n- Reformat the `Enabled()` ternary in Hook.ts to avoid ESLint-style long lines\n- Apply consistent empty-line-after-variable-declaration style to Init.ts (LandDiagnostics import, TierShim const, wrapServiceCollectionForAudit, replaceTelemetryService, createNoopTelemetryService), replacing the old convention of grouping imports before the TierShim check\n- Strip orphan blank lines from the README.md Markdown list indentation (unordered list markers now flush with 4-space indent rather than dangling)\n\nNo behavioral changes — whitespace and import ordering only.",
			"SHA": "3e010b3591ba9ad1834a07437e8eaff7ccc0960c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T22:34:56Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				359,
				2
			],
			"Message": "docs(Output): Document deep-shim tier compatibility in README and Architecture\n\nAdd a Shim Compatibility table to both `Documentation/GitHub/README.md` (new file) and `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` detailing the two-tier interception system — 🟠 Low-Level Shim (`TierShim=Own|Preempt`) for engine prototype hooks, and 🔵 Coverage Shim (`TierShim=Proxy|Replace`) for service routing and audit.\n\nAlso creates the standalone README.md for the Output Element with a concise description and cross-reference to Architecture.md, making the repository discoverable from the GitHub organization overview.\n\nThe shim documentation references `Source/Plugin/Transform/Inject/Shim/Hook.ts` as the compile-time injection site and `Source/Service/CEL/Land/Shim/` (7 files) as the runtime layer, giving downstream consumers and contributors a clear architectural map.",
			"SHA": "c4c0005856a3cc774fed567480f81f69140a7081"
